{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine","id":430576,"title":"Werewolves and the God-Machine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-06T14:09:06-08:00","id":430576,"title":"Werewolves and the God-Machine","content":"Hey guys. I'm fairly new to this whole God-Machine change, though I think I like it. My question is how do vampires and werewolves fit in? Demon is all about the machine and such, but if you wanted to use the splats together, what would be the thing that ties them all in? Sorry if it's a dumb question. I'm still working on reading my way through the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5255-willis","name":"Willis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:16:00-08:00","id":430597,"title":"","content":"They don't inherently fit in - but Vampire and Werewolf both have 2nd edition books available (Werewolf only as a pdf so far, but Vampire is orderable print on demand) with rules updated to those in also in God Machine Chronicle &amp; Demon the Descent. But the nature of Vampires and Werewolves do not metaphysically tie into the Machine as far as their lines present them, it's as complete a mystery to them as it is to most mortals - Demon is the only game that does tie in to the God Machine overtly.<br /> <br /> Mage, Promethean, and Changeling have Second Editions in the works as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:26:36-08:00","id":430610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Willis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine#post430576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys. I'm fairly new to this whole God-Machine change, though I think I like it. My question is how do vampires and werewolves fit in? Demon is all about the machine and such, but if you wanted to use the splats together, what would be the thing that ties them all in? Sorry if it's a dumb question. I'm still working on reading my way through the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping in the themes...<br /> <br /> Vampire is very...insular and usually only view things that directly deal with their nightly dramas. It much less that the God-Machine us up and about but rather how do they A) above being hit by it and B) how do they use it against their rivals.<br /> <br /> As a Demon would put it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0412628/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\">Kaneda</a>: Now you're king of the mountain, but it's all garbage!<br /> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf has the same outlook.. somewhat. If the God-Machine is up and about, expect the spirit landscape to shift depending on what projects the GM is working on. It's subtle on most projects but has to ability to nuke a local pack if it wishes.<br /> <br /> I personally am keen on the idea of the God-Machine taking note of <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Ansar-zalag</span></span> with the intent of using the <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">idigam</span></span></span> as a power source.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:27:39-08:00","id":430612,"title":"","content":"Hunter: the Vigil had a big sourcebook called &quot;Mortal Remains&quot; that recast their demons as being creatures of the God-Machine. Lot of neat ideas in that chapter - like a bounty hunting conspiracy with powers derived from angelic tattoos. Imps became Imperatives, simple god-machine processes gone awry. They don't make you sin because they're evil. They make you sin because they were designed to cause particular behaviors as part of the god-machine's plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:28:01-08:00","id":430613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Willis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine#post430576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys. I'm fairly new to this whole God-Machine change, though I think I like it. My question is how do vampires and werewolves fit in? Demon is all about the machine and such, but if you wanted to use the splats together, what would be the thing that ties them all in? Sorry if it's a dumb question. I'm still working on reading my way through the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a question the ST kind of has to answer for themselves and for their own game. Personally, my preference for Werewolf/Demon crossover is to use Macro Singe's prophecies as a base - the Crypt of the Butterfly was the Idigam's prison. From there, a lot of things fall into place pretty naturally (for me, at least).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:32:55-08:00","id":430620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=430612#post430612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter: the Vigil had a big sourcebook called &quot;Mortal Remains&quot; that recast their demons as being creatures of the God-Machine. Lot of neat ideas in that chapter - like a bounty hunting conspiracy with powers derived from angelic tattoos.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure if it really &quot;recast&quot; their Demons, or if it's more a case of them not differentiating between different &quot;things-humans-label-demons&quot; - as Inferno demons are wrapped into the same category by that Hunter-perspective chapter. I don't think the Lucifuge are blood-related to the Unchained - as we have a completely different book on the children of the Unchained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:31:11-08:00","id":430700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=430620#post430620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it really &quot;recast&quot; their Demons, or if it's more a case of them not differentiating between different &quot;things-humans-label-demons&quot; - as Inferno demons are wrapped into the same category by that Hunter-perspective chapter. I don't think the Lucifuge are blood-related to the Unchained - as we have a completely different book on the children of the Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, judging by how the Lucifage have a very diverse array of powers affecting different creatures, I always viewed them as a product of different bloodlines of various creatures that somehow intermingled, Unchained, Inferno, Fae, descents of Dhampirs etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T16:03:34-08:00","id":430745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Willis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine#post430576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys. I'm fairly new to this whole God-Machine change, though I think I like it. My question is how do vampires and werewolves fit in? Demon is all about the machine and such, but if you wanted to use the splats together, what would be the thing that ties them all in? Sorry if it's a dumb question. I'm still working on reading my way through the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iron Masters. Yeah, horrible pun fully intended, but Iron Masters consider Pretenders (term from Hunter, any supernatural being that can insinuate themselves into human society without much difficulty-ie, a playable character) to be their specialty. Most are more than human enough for the tribe to consider it safe to bring their human-hunting techniques to bare with them, Unchained and their angelic brethren not least of all (they have <i>Virtues and Vices, </i>for crying out loud!).<br /> <br /> I could easily see an Iron Master running into a ring or an angel if they notice any weird changes to their territory caused by the Machine's manipulations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T17:49:44-08:00","id":430897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=430610#post430610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally am keen on the idea of the God-Machine taking note of <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Ansar-zalag</span></span> with the intent of using the <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">idigam</span></span></span> as a power source.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yanno, I don't think I'd actually thought of that at all when I wrote it. If your game comes up with something awesome for it, and has fun with it, I'm keen to hear about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T21:18:19-08:00","id":431029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=430897#post430897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yanno, I don't think I'd actually thought of that at all when I wrote it. If your game comes up with something awesome for it, and has fun with it, I'm keen to hear about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, right now, the only game I am currently am in is a Shadowrun game.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the concept would be that the Idigam messes with the Uratha packs and protectorates and the God Machine takes note. Less that the Shadow is riled up and more a walking ball of energy is just the thing needed to power new infrastructure and bring more Angels online. Offers get sent, thing gets caught or players die, and the God Machine gets what it wants because it's the God Machine.<br /> <br /> It would be very tempting to have a Demon game running along side this with the focus of breaking the Idigam back out of it's containment (because the new infrastructure and Angels are making their lives a living &quot;hell&quot;) and having it's revenge on both the G-M cults in the area and the Uratha.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T21:32:45-08:00","id":431040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=431029#post431029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, right now, the only game I am currently am in is a Shadowrun game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you get the PM about getting the band back together?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T22:50:23-08:00","id":431077,"title":"","content":"Yes, as the others have mentioned, you don't have to integrate the god-machine into a werewolf game, think of it this way is that this world has singing cowboys, child soldiers, and martial arts master hermits, it doesn't mean they get together and fight crime.<br /> <br /> Ways to include the two if you are so inclined:<br /> <br /> Packs can now include normal humans, like say normal humans with unseen senses:god-machine.<br /> <br /> Angels can be made that eat spirits, likewise there are spirits that can eat angels.<br /> <br /> I haven't gotten to the idigam section yet, but they used to be able to manipulate essence in all sorts of ways, and angels are made out of essence, so the god-machine might help the local werewolves against the idigam.<br /> <br /> How about a lodge of iron masters centered about finding and fiddling with infrastructure? Explosions by trying to make fetishes out of infrastructure optional. <br /> <br /> While demon gives the impression that most angels are given new identities whole cloth, some of them do instead possess someone. An angel who is less than perfect in their acting skills might attract the attention of someone who is inclined to suspect possession. Likewise, some angels are inanimate objects like guns or cars or computers, so a werewolf might notice an object acting up and assume that it's a possessed object or an item with an awakened spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T02:22:23-08:00","id":431151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=431077#post431077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, as the others have mentioned, you don't have to integrate the god-machine into a werewolf game, think of it this way is that this world has singing cowboys, child soldiers, and martial arts master hermits, it doesn't mean they get together and fight crime.</div> </div> </div> </div>They would in Feng Shui!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T10:08:42-08:00","id":431387,"title":"","content":"I take it no-one's read far enough in to spot an angelic being in the text <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T10:11:24-08:00","id":431389,"title":"","content":"I remember tripping across the words machine angel somewhere, but I didn't see much of a reason to remember where. It was just a cool reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T10:17:20-08:00","id":431398,"title":"","content":"It's in the Bone Shadow tribe description as an example of things they might not be expecting on a hunt. <br /> <br /> Of note, one of the wolf-blooded tells, Piercing Eyes, allows (well, <i>forces</i>) the character to see <i>anything</i> in twilight. Ghosts, spirits, angels, the lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T10:24:19-08:00","id":431440,"title":"","content":"I was talking about another reference later in the book but there's that too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On the Bone Shadow point, you'll note from the Siskur-Dah rules that the Bone Shadow Sacred Hunt works just fine against angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T10:37:18-08:00","id":431463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=431440#post431440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was talking about another reference later in the book but there's that too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flashpoint \u2014 Lycaon-Ur and the Lodge of the Field</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not Lycaon-Ur is who he claims to be \u2014 once-King of Arcadia, turned into a werewolf by Zeus \u2014 it is undeniable that he is an ancient and terrifying predator. <b>He is eternally hungry, his maw a conduit to something else, some angelic furnace of raw Essence.</b> If he is a werewolf, then Lycaon\u2019s Primal Urge long since reached such potency that he has begun to turn into something greater. He certainly has the spiritual power to serve as patron for the lodge that has gathered around him.<br /> <br /> What happens next is anyone\u2019s guess. The Lodge of the Field is growing, and Lycaon has sent envoys to Ghost Wolves in other regions. Perhaps he hopes that it will grow enough to become a fully-fledged tribe, spurring his transfiguration on and giving him the power of a true Firstborn<b> \u2014 Devourer-Wolf, a ravenous, biomechanical hunter of metal, flesh, and lightning. </b>Maybe he hopes that enough Uratha devouring in his name, enough Essence poured down his gullet, will finally free him from his alien hunger.<br /> <br /> [\u2026]<br /> <br /> Lodge members are fanatically devoted to their holy cause, <b>fuelling the divine workings of the world itself with their consumption of human flesh.</b> They completely reject the myth of Father Wolf and Mother Luna, instead believing that <b>werewolves were placed upon the world to devour Essence and feed it to the gods.</b> Forsaken and Pure have various mocking names for them \u2014 vultures, carrion-eaters, and the like \u2014 but the Lodge of the Field remains unmoved. It spent long centuries in the shadows. <b>Now is the time for its rise.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/lespritdescalier.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:42:53-08:00","id":431661,"title":"","content":"I am sure that the fact that werewolves turn human flesh -&gt; Essence and that GMC Angels run off Essence NEVER OCCURRED TO ME AT ALL <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T13:37:04-08:00","id":431718,"title":"","content":"Well, you know, who would expect anyone to put together the obvious like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-07-2015, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T13:59:44-08:00","id":431745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=431718#post431718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you know, who would expect anyone to put together the obvious together like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, heavens forfend, be so crass as to brute-force the hunt by searching the PDF for &quot;angel&quot;? <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">:P</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:18:48-08:00","id":431844,"title":"","content":"A couple paragraphs before that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">It was also here that, in the 1500s, a human chronicler described a rain of fire striking the ground \u2014 a meteor. The lodge quickly recovered the artifice within it, an egg of lightning and gears, and delivered it to Lycaon\u2019s possession.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:46:36-08:00","id":431879,"title":"","content":"And, of course, way back by the start of the writeup for the Hunting Ground\u2026<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It came to pass that a divine being visited the hall of King Lycaon in the land of Arcadia. The visitor was tall and beautiful, a terrifying vision of grandeur in gold and silver and lightning. It strode to where the king sat on his throne, scattering his fearful sons, and told Lycaon that it had a task for him.<br /> <br /> [\u2026]<br /> <br /> \u201cThe spiritual essence of humankind lives within the body, within the heart and the meat. The gods need sacrifices to hold up the heavens and keep the world in order. For your devout obedience, I shall bless you to become a vessel for this essence, and your hunger shall become a sacrament.\u201d<br /> <br /> When the god left, Lycaon called after it, daring to name it Zeus. It said it was merely a messenger. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T17:01:43-08:00","id":432005,"title":"","content":"That's beautiful. Now I have to get the book just to throw these guys at my Demon PCs. There will be blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4832-dannyk","name":"DannyK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T18:27:58-08:00","id":432092,"title":"","content":"From all the stuff posted here, it does look like this Lycaon might be a stigmatic werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T18:55:18-08:00","id":432111,"title":"","content":"Damn, I didn't think I could want Werewolf 2e anymore, but I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T00:10:21-08:00","id":432385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=431661#post431661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sure that the fact that werewolves turn human flesh -&gt; Essence and that GMC Angels run off Essence NEVER OCCURRED TO ME AT ALL <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Well since logistically angels needs special numen to convert spiritual essence into something they can eat, there probably aren't a lot of angels that could do that.<br /> <br /> Sounds like Lycean might be one of them though.<br /> <br /> A story about demons recruiting some werewolves to help them stop (or make Lycean fall) could have possibilities. <br /> <br /> If one doesn't like the crossover, well the shapeshifters from war against the pure could certainly include cannibal werewolves cursed by Zeus, so it could be run as the werewolves being infiltrated by lycans. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T00:22:43-08:00","id":432393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=432385#post432385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well since logistically angels needs special numen to convert spiritual essence into something they can eat, there probably aren't a lot of angels that could do that.<br /> <br /> Sounds like Lycean might be one of them though.<br /> <br /> A story about demons recruiting some werewolves to help them stop (or make Lycean fall) could have possibilities.<br /> <br /> If one doesn't like the crossover, well the shapeshifters from war against the pure could certainly include cannibal werewolves cursed by Zeus, so it could be run as the werewolves being infiltrated by lycans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still trying to process what just Lycean is. Angel, not so much if the story is taken at face value due to more human like characteristics. Uratha, most likely but I don't know if the GM could make a person a Uratha at all, let alone on the spot.<br /> <br /> The meteor is most likely infrastructure while Lycean himself is a Uratha that is either a GM experiment (Uratha with Angel parts being put in) or simply a cult leader who the GM sends visions of power and rapture to.<br /> <br /> Most likely idea in my mind is Meteor is where all the Essence is dumped to the GM. Lycean heads an GM cult build on consuming humans for essence, and them dumps it into that Meteor for the GM to use.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T05:23:19-07:00","id":432527,"title":"","content":"Considering that even archmasters can't make a werewolf without Luna's permission, I'd go with a solid no. <br /> <br /> Furthermore, if he's King Lycean then he's over 2400 years old, which is a bit much even with werewolves having an indeterminate lifespan. <br /> <br /> And hes the spiritual patron of a lodge. So either he's a werewolf/angel/spirit, at which point he should think about being a ninja zombie pirate to boot, or he's an angel faking lycanthropic and spiritual traits.<br /> <br /> You can certainly do what you want in your games, but I'm going to in favor of occam's razor here. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T05:29:29-07:00","id":432536,"title":"","content":"I think they can make one but can't <i>un</i>-make one. I know the vampire patron is fine with you making more vampires. It's curing one it throws a shit fit about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T05:32:38-07:00","id":432549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=432527#post432527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Considering that even archmasters can't make a werewolf without Luna's permission, I'd go with a solid no.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be too concerned about what the rules for a different game line say Archmasters can or cannot do when considering who and what Lycaon-Ur is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T07:26:04-07:00","id":432607,"title":"","content":"When the line is to the effect that werewolves are Luna's property and anyone who messes with them in a way she doesn't like she'll go cut a bitch, I'd say yes it is relevant.<br /> <br /> Why should Luna get more respect in a mage game than a werewolf one?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=432536#post432536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they can make one but can't <i>un</i>-make one. I know the vampire patron is fine with you making more vampires. It's curing one it throws a shit fit about.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, because they have tacit permission. If your goal is to make a trojan wolf that will turn her children into nothing more than cannibalistic essence factories for the god-machine, well Luna's nuts, but I think that's back into cut a bitch territory. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 03-08-2015, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T07:47:26-07:00","id":432620,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the relationship between Archmages and Luna is not necessarily the same as the one between the God-Machine and Luna. Perhaps Luna has trouble cutting that particular kind of bitch or maybe the two even have some kind of deal (she is known for being a bit... erratic after all, who knows what goes on in her pretty head). Maybe her cutting that bitch is still a work in process. Maybe the whole deal with Lycaon-ur is hidden by very powerful Infrastructure shielding it from cosmic perception/interference.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T07:57:31-07:00","id":432623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=432607#post432607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the line is to the effect that werewolves are Luna's property and anyone who messes with them in a way she doesn't like she'll go cut a bitch, I'd say yes it is relevant.<br /> <br /> Why should Luna get more respect in a mage game than a werewolf one?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is still not relevant for ground level play. Assuming the situation is what it is you can think of a lot of reasons for this happening without disrespecting the power of Luna. Maybe Luna does not think this small infringement to be important on the large scale. For example the Pure alter Werewolf templates all the time by excising Auspices and Luna also doesn't directly smite them. And even if Luna does care about this one Werewolf cult, maybe the God Machine or one of its Angels cut Luna a deal to look the other way. Or Luna is just busy adressing more pressing matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T09:37:19-07:00","id":432674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=432607#post432607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the line is to the effect that werewolves are Luna's property and anyone who messes with them in a way she doesn't like she'll go cut a bitch, I'd say yes it is relevant.<br /> <br /> Why should Luna get more respect in a mage game than a werewolf one?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies, my one line response probably didn't have much clarity to it.<br /> <br /> It is entirely ok to run with the content of Imperial Mysteries if a group wants. However, the approach that Imperial Mysteries takes to looking at such elements is not relevant to the <i>baseline</i> approach for Werewolf. You don't need Imperial Mysteries to run Werewolf, to decide how the high-level elements of the setting interact, and what is or is not possible.<br /> <br /> Consider Lycaon-Ur and his origin story entirely within the scope of Werewolf itself. Rules for templates and the creation thereof from an entirely different gameline are not something that it's worth getting hung up over in the face of what makes the best story for Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Just within Werewolf, Lycaon-Ur provides a different origin story for werewolves that clashes with the main, orthodox beliefs of Forsaken and Pure. He offers a take on the classic myths of Lykaeon, plays up the cannibalism elements of the Uratha state and offers some possible explanation for <i>why</i> Uratha gain Essence from consuming human flesh. He offers a potential example of what happens when a werewolf hits Primal Urge 10 and just keeps on going up. He may also be a massive, massive liar.<br /> <br /> You don't even need to draw on the God-Machine or Demon for explanations as to what's going on. If Lycaon is telling the truth, there is <i>some kind of power</i>at work consuming Essence. You can, of course, decide to plug Lycaon directly into those mythologies but it's not necessary.<br /> <br /> Within Werewolf itself, having alternate origin stories for werewolves is not offering Luna less 'respect', any more than bringing in an optional supplement from a different gameline would be giving Luna more. Taking a look at another line for a moment, whatever Imperial Mysteries has to say about some sort of 'sponsor' for vampires, the fact that they're now depicted with a heavy slant towards the Clans all having different origins stands as its own thing.<br /> <br /> The Quicksilver Children believe <i>idigam</i> made Uratha. They might be right. So might the Pure &amp; Forsaken, <i>and</i> Lycaon. There may be several different sources of werewolves, or a repeating phenomena that's the same thing, or Luna working through various mediums to create new batches several times, or something else entirely...<br /> <br /> tl;dr version: Don't rely on Imperial Mysteries to understand what's going on. Lycaon-Ur is a freestanding thing within Werewolf and doesn't need to rely on other lines to explain it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T09:59:09-07:00","id":432694,"title":"","content":"Of course, an Imperial Mysteries game dealing with some of the most potent Idigam could be fun. Though that's perhaps slightly off topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T10:31:48-07:00","id":432721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=431029#post431029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, right now, the only game I am currently am in is a Shadowrun game.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the concept would be that the Idigam messes with the Uratha packs and protectorates and the God Machine takes note. Less that the Shadow is riled up and more a walking ball of energy is just the thing needed to power new infrastructure and bring more Angels online. Offers get sent, thing gets caught or players die, and the God Machine gets what it wants because it's the God Machine.<br /> <br /> It would be very tempting to have a Demon game running along side this with the focus of breaking the Idigam back out of it's containment (because the new infrastructure and Angels are making their lives a living &quot;hell&quot;) and having it's revenge on both the G-M cults in the area and the Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that would be rather cool, actually. I may actually steal that idea for my own game, if that's alright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T23:06:19-07:00","id":433618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=432620#post432620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe her cutting that bitch is still a work in process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence the Player Characters and perhaps a Sliver Crusade story.<br /> <br /> That being said, Luna is still a distant God. Hence why the Pure haven't been killed off and perhaps largely busy dealing with trying to keep track of Idigam escaping. <br /> <br /> Not to mention the one that is currently wearing her dead lover's face which I'm sure has her full attention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430576-werewolves-and-the-god-machine?p=432674#post432674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just within Werewolf, Lycaon-Ur provides a different origin story for werewolves that clashes with the main, orthodox beliefs of Forsaken and Pure. He offers a take on the classic myths of Lykaeon, plays up the cannibalism elements of the Uratha state and offers some possible explanation for <i>why</i> Uratha gain Essence from consuming human flesh. He offers a potential example of what happens when a werewolf hits Primal Urge 10 and just keeps on going up. He may also be a massive, massive liar.<br /> <br /> You don't even need to draw on the God-Machine or Demon for explanations as to what's going on. If Lycaon is telling the truth, there is <i>some kind of power</i>at work consuming Essence. You can, of course, decide to plug Lycaon directly into those mythologies but it's not necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Plug Lycaon directly into&quot;<br /> <br /> Hehe.<br /> <br /> Anyways. I like the story and I still think that Lycaon is a Uratha that was approached to set up a Lodge for the GM (an Arch Angel behind the thing) in the same vein that the VtR's Holy Engineers are.<br /> <br /> But f course, the GM is nWoD's Cthulhu and while Cthulhu is great for a Mythos game, even the Mythos knows when it pull it back a tad so Lycaon simply may just be lying or someone saw a Demon in the area doing something entirely unrelated and mistook it for Lycaon or perhaps it's a story that an Iron Master cooked up when he thought &quot;A wolf shall hunt&quot; included taking a load of questionable chemicals and &quot;Chase the Dragon&quot;. <br /> <br /> Iron Masters sure are a shifty lot aren't they?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}